| Static virtual-determinant payment by `G+E+O(B)` | regression | Connected two-grain oblique-lattice disk: `M_inter=Theta(m^2)` while `G+E+B=Theta(m)`; it is not globally optimal |
| A non-atomic train population may remain linear | handled | It is excluded from positive quadratic crossing mass by Section 39.1; the proof retains it in the total (T) and uses only (T=O(D)) |
| Dense graph alone does not give a biclique | handled | The extraction uses promoted geometric interval theorem IS, not generic graph density |
| A coherent local block need not carry the global core | handled at this equality case | Equality in the global atomic Mantel bound forces the selected atomic subgraph to carry (R-o(D^2)) crossings |
| Local or feasible configurations do not imply global optimality | respected | The result assumes global minimizers throughout and gives no Level I conclusion outside the pure-disk branch |
| Section 39 support depth cannot be counted as independent Oler surplus | not used | No support-depth-to-Oler conversion appears in the proof |
| GPI near-balance estimate used without global-core coverage | rejected and corrected | GPI Lemma GPI.1 is proved by contradiction using the global-core upper bound; statements (2.7)–(2.8) instead split by class balance |

