## 9. Computation

`python3 research/verify_target_b_zero_deficit_aggregate_arithmetic_2026_10_10.py`
reproduces the four exact allocation values and certifies their maximum is
`72689/549081 < 0.1324`. It also verifies the absolute and relative train-ratio
consequences separately, and rejects the former false decimal chain using
rational Machin enclosures of pi. The script assumes the analytic share caps;
it does not verify their geometric premises. The separate constant comparison used
for the atomic Mantel endpoint is exact and follows from
\(27\pi>81>64>32\sqrt3\).

`python3 research/verify_target_b_connected_notch_regression_2026_10_15.py`
checks the analogous rational basis `(1,0),(5/13,12/13)` for `m=4,5,8`.
It examines every source pair and actual contact, the cell boundary and train
counts, the two missing opposite-block crossing families, the diameter and
hull gap, and a same-cardinality square-grid competitor. A one-column-notch
mutation is rejected because it has additional actual unit contacts. These
finite fixtures do not certify the transcendental sequence `theta_m`, its
asymptotic estimates, or global optimality. Both checkers refuse optimized
Python because their exact checks require assertions.

## 10. Corrections / supersessions

The initially drafted finite-threshold claim \(\rho\ge0.674\) was withdrawn:
its use of the GPI near-balance estimate was circular outside the core-carrying
scope. Statements (2.7)–(2.8) use an explicit imbalanced/balanced split and
do not import that estimate. These candidates sharpen the equality-case
conclusion of Section 39 but do not supersede any canonical inequality.

The autonomous PR #949 audit on 2026-10-15 corrected the false intermediate
comparison `2.6167 > 1.0304 x0`, separated the two valid bounds, renamed a
local center-class mass that shadowed `c`, and synchronized the finite-window
table with the proof's split at `5e-8 tau`. See the
[substantive audit](../audits/pr949_autonomous_proof_audit_2026-10-15.md).

